<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE kinetica2-y2 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Kinetica-2 Y2 / SpaceSail (Qianfan) polar group (Jiuquan LA-140) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Event times: CAS Space TYPICAL Kinetica-2 sequence (Y1 documentary) via https://sat.huijiwiki.com/wiki/力箭二号: fairing sep 217.73 s, S2 cutoff 493.71 s; S1 cutoff 180 s ASSUMED (upper bound from 720 s test time &gt;= 4x flight time).
Azimuth 186.58 deg: mean great-circle bearing from pad to NOTAM ZLHW A5561/26 (32.625N 99.042E, 186.93 deg) and ZPKM A5562/26 (30.367N 98.904E, 186.24 deg) area centroids (https://www.space-notices.com/); implies i~95.0 deg.
Orbit unpublished: S2-cutoff altitude 500 km ASSUMED (= published 8 t to 500 km SSO reference). Payload: 18 Qianfan per SatNet News (UNOFFICIAL, https://satnet.news/item/76103); near-polar per https://www.unilym.com/articles/lijian-2-yao2-18xing-20261102 (unofficial).
T0: LL2 NET 2026-11-03T00:10:00Z (window 00:05-00:33Z = Mon 2 Nov 4:10 pm PST); SatNet window BJT 3 Nov 08:00-09:00.
Altitude knots (t s: km; times published typical sequence, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times, final = assumed orbit): 0:0, 180:95.8, 217.73:149.7, 493.71:500
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.653 km/s (circular v at 500 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+493.71 s. File ends at final cutoff.
Pad (LL2): 40.817480N 100.219390E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=186.58 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-03T00:10:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
